# LookupSelect

Record fields use `LookupSelect` from `@/components/lookup`, or a variant built on it: `AccountLookup`, `ContactLookup`, `ProductLookup`, `TaxLookup`, `TrackingLookup`, `BankLookup`.

Use the native `Select` only for a short fixed enumeration (status, tax-inclusive/exclusive, month, locale).

## Required behaviour

- Search code, name, SKU, description and other identifiers. Select by record id.
- Group with category headings. Show `code — name` when a code exists.
- Include `+ Create new` only when the user may create and a real save path exists. Open that form in `LookupCreateFlyover` (or the existing sheet the screen already uses). Keep the parent form, prefill from the search text, refresh, select the new id, and return focus. Cancelling or a failed save leaves the previous value in place.
- Show loading, empty and error (with retry) states. Support clear when the field may be empty, plus required, disabled and invalid.
- Page or server-search large lists with `useLookupQuery` (debounced, aborted, cached, scoped by `companyId`).
- Hide or disable records the active organisation, role, active flag, account type, tax date, currency or posting rule does not allow. The server functions remain the authority; do not weaken them to make a lookup succeed.

```tsx
<AccountLookup
  accounts={accounts}
  companyId={companyId}
  value={accountId}
  onChange={setAccountId}
  ariaLabel="Account"
/>
```
